From 2a73b02e409f6560cb920b4c45399b4ad9a0be77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:09:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/31] WIP qsa3: fuse the pack into one launcher pass (session
 7)

The graph built pk/pv as cast + permute + cont + reshape + permute + cont -
three copy passes over the cache, the two conts element-scalar
(cpy_scalar<half,half> 41 ms + cpy_scalar_transpose 9.5 ms at pp8192).

The graph now only materialises the natural contiguous F16 view
[D=256, n_head_kv, n_kv]; two new launcher kernels do the whole re-layout in
one pass each:
  qsa3_pack_keys_kernel / qsa3_pack_values_kernel.

Bit-identical (pure permutation of the same F16 values):
  PPL c2048 bf16 10.5771 both builds
  greedy sha=04ddb94b1529 (665 chars) both builds
  test-backend-ops FLASH_ATTN_QSA / FLASH_ATTN_EXT green

pp8192 (IQ4_XS, -b/-ub 2048):
  bf16 KV 966.8 -> 968.75 t/s;  pack kernels 50.5 -> 6.5 ms (save 43.96 ms = 0.26 %)
  q8_0 KV 953.6 -> 959.0 t/s;   pack chain   86.4 -> 49.1 ms (save 37.34 ms = 0.22 %)
  f16  KV unchanged path, works (954.5 t/s)

The F16/BF16 cast (bf16 7.7 ms) and the quantized->F16 chain (q8_0 35 ms)
stay as graph ops; fusing them is <0.05 % for the default bf16 config.
